{
  "subject": "Basic Mathematics",
  "topic": "Trigonometry",
  "introduction": "Trigonometry deals with relationships between angles and sides in triangles, as well as periodic functions. In SIMAK, key areas include: trig identities, max/min values of trig expressions, and solving trig equations. The unit circle and key angle values (30°,45°,60°) must be memorized.",
  "key_formulas": [
    {
      "name": "Pythagorean identity",
      "formula": "\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1"
    },
    {
      "name": "Double angle (sin)",
      "formula": "\\sin 2\\theta = 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta"
    },
    {
      "name": "Double angle (cos)",
      "formula": "\\cos 2\\theta = \\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta = 1-2\\sin^2\\theta"
    },
    {
      "name": "Max of a·cos+b·sin",
      "formula": "\\max(a\\cos\\theta + b\\sin\\theta) = \\sqrt{a^2+b^2}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sum-to-product",
      "formula": "\\sin A + \\sin B = 2\\sin\\frac{A+B}{2}\\cos\\frac{A-B}{2}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Law of Cosines",
      "formula": "c^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\\cos C"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tan identity",
      "formula": "\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}, \\quad 1+\\tan^2\\theta = \\sec^2\\theta"
    }
  ],
  "tips_and_tricks": [
    "Memorize: sin30°=1/2, sin45°=√2/2, sin60°=√3/2, sin90°=1.",
    "Max of a·sinθ+b·cosθ is always √(a²+b²). Min is -√(a²+b²).",
    "cos2θ = 1-2sin²θ: use to convert cos² problems to sin².",
    "sin²θ = (1-cos2θ)/2 and cos²θ = (1+cos2θ)/2 (power reduction).",
    "CAST rule: All positive in Q1, Sin positive in Q2, Tan in Q3, Cos in Q4.",
    "sin(π-x) = sinx; cos(π-x) = -cosx; sin(-x) = -sinx."
  ],
  "worked_examples": [
    {
      "title": "Example 1: Maximum of trig expression",
      "question": "Find the maximum value of f(x) = 3sin(x) + 4cos(x) + 5.",
      "solution": [
        "Step 1: Max of a·sin+b·cos = √(a²+b²).",
        "Step 2: √(3²+4²) = √(9+16) = √25 = 5.",
        "Step 3: Max of 3sin(x)+4cos(x) = 5.",
        "Step 4: Max of f(x) = 5+5 = 10."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Example 2: Simplifying with identities",
      "question": "Simplify: (sin²x - cos²x)/(sinx - cosx).",
      "solution": [
        "Step 1: Factor numerator: sin²x-cos²x = (sinx-cosx)(sinx+cosx).",
        "Step 2: Cancel (sinx-cosx) (valid when sinx≠cosx).",
        "Step 3: Result = sinx+cosx."
      ]
    }
  ],
